<article class="env-remark" id="09A4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09A4">Remark <span data-tag="09A4">61.14.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Because $X_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}$ has enough weakly contractible objects for all $K$ in $D(X_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale})$ we have $K = R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits \tau _{\geq -n}K$ by Cohomology on Sites, Proposition <a href="/tag/0947" data-tag="0947">21.51.2</a>. Since $R\Gamma $ commutes with $R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits $ by Injectives, Lemma <a href="/tag/08U1" data-tag="08U1">19.13.6</a> we see that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R\Gamma (X, K) = R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits R\Gamma (X, \tau _{\geq -n}K)  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(\textit{Ab})$. This will sometimes allow us to extend results from bounded below complexes to all complexes. </p>
</article>